The sink copies a decoded frame into dumb buffers of the DRM device, one byte
per pixel. virtio-gpu makes dumb buffers of 32 bits per pixel only, so the
request failed there, and the sink then wrote the frame to an address that was
not mapped (a segmentation fault in the stream's thread). With
WST_DUMB_BYTES_PER_PIXEL=4 the same bytes are asked for as a 32-bit buffer.

Upstream-Status: Pending

